eta` and `sunset` kinds survive; and the five live[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]flag beads are migrated in place.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]9[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]flag_task_type.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Free the `flag` task-type slug[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]slug[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]slug: drop `flag` from the Rust core's reserved task-type slug list so a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project may claim it, leaving the issue type untouched.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Declare the `flag` task type in project config[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]type[dim] · [dim][/dim]after slug[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]type: add the seven-field `flag` task-type spec to `bead.task_types` in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]this repo's project config, pin its glyph and accent, and refresh the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]committed catalog snapshot.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Two kinds, a derived default, and a rebuilt `sase flag new`[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after type[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: collapse the flag kinds to `beta` and `sunset`, derive the registry[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default and drop scope, and make `sase flag new` create the typed task [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead from three required prose arguments.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Due-ness, identity, and integrity read task-type fields[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]reads[dim] · [dim][/dim]after type[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reads: repoint every flag-domain read path — due-state, the key and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]countdown chips, bead loading, registry integrity, the doctor, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lint — from `issue.flag` to the typed task bead's field values.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]FlagTriage is a task-bead gate[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gates[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reads[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gates: make the reconciler and the FlagTriage contract select and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]describe flag beads by task type, and replace pending gates that still [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]carry the old payload.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Every bead surface renders a flag as a typed task[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reads[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]surfaces: move the ACE beads pane, bead pages, CLI listings and detail, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the mobile helper, the external mirror, and the stale-cleanup and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]duplicate-scan carve-outs onto the task type.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate the five live flag beads[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]migrate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli, gates, surfaces[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate: rewrite the five existing flag bead event streams in place into[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]typed task beads with hand-authored field values, then regenerate the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]projection, the mirror, and the pages.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Delete the `flag` issue type end to end[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]retire[dim] · [dim][/dim]after migrate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]retire: remove the flag issue type, `FlagRecord`, and `BeadFlagWire` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from the Rust wire, the Python model, the storage codecs, the create [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]grammar, and the compatibility mirror schema.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory notes, generated instructions, and documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after retire[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: rewrite the two feature-flag memory notes, regenerate the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instruction files and catalog snapshot, and update every doc page that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]still describes a flag bead type.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-pv","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-pv.4","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-f4eb17f50ae1c2198ca5e1d13a453051","started_at":"2026-08-18T17:28:09.824367+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"18c11e229740ab288d00a9cedb6cfa388edc65d5784e698369174e04636e73fc","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-pv.5/chat.md","size_bytes":7127},"commits":{"digest":"12e013ee3e081c6a9526a5ce9489582b59592a2d52f94f4b0bd95dde00b3cbd6","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-pv.5/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-pv.5/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"afe708dfdc1814b07dcf4eb5e0c783d7b58fdb8b89c246447cc24694aaa07e3f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-pv.5/meta.json","size_bytes":633},"prompt":{"digest":"a047292bd6c14b11f8420c6dc75a1e47